codex
Implemented REL-RC-J and REL-RC-G2. No commit made.

Summary:
- `finish.py`: `_last_productive_seq` now counts only productive actions with paired successful observations.
- `signals.py`: execution-gate productive checks now use the same successful-observation rule so failed actions do not satisfy the finish gate.
- `files.py`: insert guards now pass covered `edit_lines`; refusal full-read cap raised to 64KB; anchored edit callers now get full refusal-read delivery up to 64KB and no content above that.
- Added regressions for failed productive actions, insert retry recovery, anchored edit retry recovery, large anchored no-content refusal, and blind write still blocked.

Verification:
- Requested command failed only on an environment-bound existing test:
  `test_app_verify_command_distinguishes_serving_from_not` fails with `PermissionError: [Errno 1] Operation not permitted` on `socket.socket()`.
- Same selection excluding that socket test passes:
  `.venv/bin/python3 -m pytest ... -k '(finish or nudge or productive) and not app_verify_command_distinguishes_serving_from_not' -q`
- `git diff --check` passed.

